description:
Design a clock control circuit that acts as a clock edge detector and a signal filter. The module takes an input clock signal (`inclk`) and an enable signal (`ena`) to produce a filtered clock output (`outclk`). When `ena` is high, the circuit monitors the clock's rising edges. It uses a 2-bit state register to track transitions, generating a high output on `outclk` for one clock cycle when a rising edge is detected, effectively filtering the clock to remove unwanted glitches. When `ena` is low, the output is forced to LOW.
module top_module(
    input inclk,
    input ena,
    output outclk
);

code:
module top_module(
    input inclk,
    input ena,
    output outclk
);reg [1:0] state;
reg filtered_clk;

always @(posedge inclk) begin
    if (ena) begin
        state <= {state[0], inclk};
        if (state == 2'b01) begin
            filtered_clk <= 1'b1;
        end else if (state == 2'b10) begin
            filtered_clk <= 1'b0;
        end
    end else begin
        filtered_clk <= 1'b0;
    end
end

assign outclk = filtered_clk;

endmodule

