Design a Power-On Reset (POR) circuit that generates a reset signal when power is applied. The module takes a clock signal and a power-on indication as inputs. Upon detecting the power-on signal, it asserts a reset signal for a specified duration, ensuring the system initializes correctly before normal operation. The reset signal remains active while being held high after power is applied, then transitions low after the designated reset time, allowing proper initialization of other components in the circuit.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input pwr_on,
  output reg rst
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input pwr_on,
  output reg rst
);parameter reset_time = 100; // length of time for reset signal to be active

reg reset_pulse; // pulse signal used to generate reset signal

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (pwr_on) begin
    reset_pulse <= 1'b1;
    rst <= 1'b1;
  end else if (reset_pulse) begin
    reset_pulse <= 1'b0;
    rst <= 1'b0;
  end
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (reset_pulse) begin
    #reset_time;
    reset_pulse <= 1'b0;
  end
end

endmodule

