description:
Design a debouncer circuit that stabilizes a potentially noisy input signal. This module detects transitions in the input signal and only changes its output after a specified debounce time, which is defined in terms of clock cycles. When a rising edge is detected on the input (from low to high), the circuit initiates a countdown that holds the output high for the duration of the debounce time. If no further transitions occur during this time, the output remains high; otherwise, it resets to low upon detecting a low input or after the debounce time expires. The circuit thereby ensures that transient fluctuations of the input do not cause unintended rapid changes at the output.
module top_module(
  input clk,          // Added clock input
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,          // Added clock input
  input in,
  output out
);parameter debounce_time = 100; // debounce time in clock cycles (change as needed)
parameter clock_period = 10; // clock period in nanoseconds (change as needed)

reg [debounce_time-1:0] debounce_counter;
reg out_reg;
reg in_last;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (in_last == 1'b0 && in == 1'b1) begin // detect rising edge
    debounce_counter <= debounce_time;
  end else if (debounce_counter > 0) begin // debounce time
    debounce_counter <= debounce_counter - 1;
  end else if (in == 1'b1) begin // set output
    out_reg <= 1'b1;
  end else begin // reset
    out_reg <= 1'b0;
  end
  in_last <= in;
end

assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

