description:
Design a bit extender that takes a 16-bit input and produces a 32-bit output. If the most significant bit (MSB) of the input is 1 (indicating a negative value in two's complement representation), the MSB is extended by padding the upper 16 bits with zeros, thus replicating the sign bit. If the MSB is 0, the output retains the original 16 bits with the upper 16 bits being zeros.
module top_module(
	input16,
	output32
);

code:
module top_module(
	input16,
	output32
);input [15:0] input16;
	output reg [31:0] output32;

	always @ ( * ) begin
		output32 = input16;
		if(input16[15] == 1'b1) begin
			output32 = {16'b0000000000000000, input16};
		end
	end
endmodule

