description:
Design a Schmitt trigger circuit that implements hysteresis for improved noise immunity on an input signal. The circuit has defined threshold levels, VL for low and VH for high, which determine when the output transitions between high (1) and low (0). The output changes state based on the input signal's relation to these thresholds and incorporates a hysteresis effect, ensuring stable output when the input signal fluctuates around the threshold values. This functionality is crucial in applications where clean signal transitions are necessary despite noisy input conditions.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output reg out
);parameter VL = 1; // low threshold value
parameter VH = 3; // high threshold value
parameter hysteresis = 1; // hysteresis value

reg prev_out; // previous output state

always @(in) begin
  if (in > VH) begin
    out = 1;
  end else if (in < VL) begin
    out = 0;
  end else if (in > (prev_out + hysteresis)) begin
    out = 1;
  end else if (in < (prev_out - hysteresis)) begin
    out = 0;
  end
  prev_out = out;
end

endmodule

