description:
Design a n-bit wide ring counter that generates a shifting output pattern in response to a clock signal. The counter increments its count on each positive edge of the clock, and when it reaches its maximum value, it resets back to zero. The output reflects the current state of the counter, where each output bit is derived from the previous output bit, effectively shifting the active bit through the output lines. This design is useful for applications requiring cyclical counting or rotating signal generation.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] count;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  count <= count + 1;
  if (count == 2**n) begin
    count <= 0;
  end
end

assign out[0] = count[0];
generate
  genvar i;
  for (i = 1; i < n; i = i + 1) begin
    assign out[i] = out[i-1];
  end
endgenerate

endmodule

